  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 1407.04 Labeling and Packaging",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 1407.04 Labeling and Packaging. Prior to and during transportation, a used oil transporter shall ensure that each container holding used oil is:\n\n(a) Clearly labeled or marked with:\n\n(1) The words “used oil”; and\n\n(2) All applicable US DOT required information as set forth in 49 CFR Part 172;\n\n(b) Secured against movement within the vehicle if the container holding used oil is not a part of the vehicle; and\n\n(c) Sealed to prevent releases.\n\nSource. #14282, eff 8-1-25, EXPIRES: 8-1-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html"
}
